Ram disk memory type for loader.efi memdisk=: never EfiLoaderData, so the
kernel does not reclaim a ram disk root.  A buffer registered with
EFI_RAM_DISK_PROTOCOL is EfiReservedMemoryType (ACPI NFIT rule for virtual
disks); a buffer only md uses (no RamDisk protocol, and initmd) gets the OS
loader type 0x80000000, since UEFI forbids loaders to allocate Reserved.
Needs md_preload_mapdev.patch in the booted kernel when the ram disk can
land above the direct map.

Bug report: FreeBSD/docs/bugreport_loader_memdisk_memtype.md
Investigation: FreeBSD/iPXE.md, section 7(f) "The fallback needed four fixes"

